Acts 15:2), although his name nowhere occurs in the Acts of the Apostles.","verses":12,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"demas_1006","name":"Demas","also":"","summary":"A companion and fellow-labourer of Paul during his first imprisonment at Rome (Philemon 1:24; Col. 4:14).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"crescens_960","name":"Crescens","also":"","summary":"Increasing, probably one of the seventy disciples of Christ.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"mark_1679","name":"John","also":"Marcus","summary":"The evangelist; “John whose surname was Mark” (Acts 12:12, 25). Mark (Marcus, Col. 4:10, etc.) was his Roman name, which gradually came to supersede his Jewish name John.","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"Mary","v":[11]},{"id":"luke_1836","name":"Luke","also":"Lucas","summary":"The evangelist, was a Gentile. The date and circumstances of his conversion are unknown. According to his own statement (Luke 1:2), he was not an “eye-witness and minister of the word from the beginning.”","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"tychicus_2885","name":"Tychicus","also":"","summary":"Chance, an Asiatic Christian, a “faithful minister in the Lord” (Eph. 6:21, 22), who, with Trophimus, accompanied Paul on a part of his journey from Macedonia to Jerusalem (Acts 20:4).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"alexander_189","name":"Alexander","also":"","summary":"A coppersmith who, with Hymenaeus and others, promulgated certain heresies regarding the resurrection (1 Tim. 1:19; 2 Tim. 4:14), and made shipwreck of faith and of a good conscience.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"aquila_279","name":"Aquila","also":"","summary":"Eagle, a native of Pontus, by occupation a tent-maker, whom Paul met on his first visit to Corinth (Acts 18:2). Along with his wife Priscilla he had fled from Rome in consequence of a decree (A.D. 50) by Claudius commanding all Jews to leave the city.","verses":6,"father":"","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"priscilla_2370","name":"Priscilla","also":"Prisca","summary":"The wife of Aquila (Acts 18:2), who is never mentioned without her. Her name sometimes takes the precedence of his (Rom. 16:3; 2 Tim. 4:19).","verses":6,"father":"","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"onesiphorus_2252","name":"Onesiphorus","also":"","summary":"Bringing profit, an Ephesian Christian who showed great kindness to Paul at Rome. He served him in many things, and had oft refreshed him.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"erastus_1213","name":"Erastus","also":"","summary":"A companion of Paul at Ephesus, who was sent by him along with Timothy into Macedonia (Acts 19:22).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"trophimus_2880","name":"Trophimus","also":"","summary":"A foster-child, an Ephesian who accompanied Paul during a part of his third missionary journey (Acts 20:4; 21:29). He was with Paul in Jerusalem, and the Jews, supposing that the apostle had brought him with him into the temple, raised a tumult which resulted in Paul’s imprisonment.","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"claudia_946","name":"Claudia","also":"","summary":"A female Christian mentioned in 2 Tim. 4:21.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"eubulus_1227","name":"Eubulus","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"linus_1826","name":"Linus","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"pudens_2375","name":"Pudens","also":"","summary":"Bashful, a Christian at Rome, who sent his greetings to Timothy (2 Tim. 4:21).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]}],"places":[{"id":"dalmatia_321","name":"Dalmatia","kind":"Region","lat":43.51548,"lon":16.07154,"summary":"A mountainous country on the eastern shore of the Adriatic, a part of the Roman province of Illyricum. It still bears its ancient name. During Paul’s second imprisonment at Rome, Titus left him to visit Dalmatia (2 Tim. 4:10) for some unknown purpose.","verses":1,"v":[10]},{"id":"galatia_431","name":"Galatia","kind":"Region","lat":37.5,"lon":32.5,"summary":"Has been called the “Gallia” of the East, Roman writers calling its inhabitants Galli. They were an intermixture of Gauls and Greeks, and hence were called Gallo-Graeci, and the country Gallo-Graecia.","verses":6,"v":[10]},{"id":"thessalonica_1158","name":"Thessalonica","kind":"City","lat":40.63028,"lon":22.94957,"summary":"A large and populous city on the Thermaic bay. It was the capital of one of the four Roman districts of Macedonia, and was ruled by a praetor.","verses":6,"v":[10]},{"id":"ephesus_400","name":"Ephesus","kind":"City","lat":37.94194,"lon":27.33972,"summary":"The capital of proconsular Asia, which was the western part of Asia Minor. It was colonized principally from Athens. In the time of the Romans it bore the title of “the first and greatest metropolis of Asia.”","verses":17,"v":[12]},{"id":"troas_1182","name":"Troas","kind":"City","lat":39.75135,"lon":26.15765,"summary":"A city on the coast of Mysia, in the north-west of Asia Minor, named after ancient Troy, which was at some little distance from it (about 4 miles) to the north.","verses":6,"v":[13]},{"id":"corinth_306","name":"Corinth","kind":"City","lat":37.90604,"lon":22.87872,"summary":"A Grecian city, on the isthmus which joins the Peloponnesus to the mainland of Greece. It is about 48 miles west of Athens. The ancient city was destroyed by the Romans (B.C. 146), and that mentioned in the New Testament was quite a new city, having been rebuilt about a century afterwards and peopled by a colony of freedmen from Rome.","verses":6,"v":[20]},{"id":"miletus_801","name":"Miletus","kind":"City","lat":37.52924,"lon":27.27749,"summary":"(Miletum, 2 Tim. 4:20), a seaport town and the ancient capital of Ionia, about 36 miles south of Ephesus. On his voyage from Greece to Syria, Paul touched at this port, and delivered that noble and pathetic address to the elders (“presbyters,” ver. 28) of Ephesus recorded in Acts 20:15-35.","verses":3,"v":[20]}],"events":[],"traditions":[["healing-today",20,20]],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1263,1263,1263,1799,1799,1799,2316,2316,2532,5547,5547,2424,3588,3195,2919,2198,2198,2532,3498,3498,2532,2532,2532,846,846,2015,2532,846,932],[2784,3588,3056,2186,2186,2122,2122,171,171,171,171,1651,2008,3870,3870,1722,3956,3956,3956,3115,1322],[1063,2540,2540,1510,1510,3753,430,430,430,430,5198,1319,235,2833,2833,189,2002,2002,2002,2002,1438,1320,2596,2596,3588,2398,1939],[2532,654,654,654,3588,189,189,575,3588,225,1161,1624,1624,1909,3454],[1161,4771,3525,3525,1722,3956,3956,2553,2553,4160,2041,2041,2099,2099,2099,4135,4771,1248],[1063,1473,1473,2235,4689,4689,4689,4689,4689,4689,4689,2532,3588,2540,3588,1473,359,2186,2186,2186],[75,75,75,3588,2570,73,5055,5055,5055,3588,1408,5083,5083,5083,3588,4102],[3063,3063,3063,606,606,606,606,1473,1473,3588,4735,1343,1343,3739,3588,2962,3588,1342,2923,591,591,1473,1473,1722,1565,2250,3756,3440,1473,1473,235,3956,3956,3588,25,846,2015],[4704,4704,4704,2064,2064,4314,1473,5030],[1063,1214,25,25,25,25,3568,165,1459,1459,1473,2532,4198,1519,2332,2913,2913,2913,1519,1053,5103,5103,1519,1149],[3441,3065,1510,3326,1473,353,3138,71,71,71,3326,4572,1063,1510,1510,2173,1473,1473,1519,1248,1248],[5190,1161,649,649,649,1519,2181],[2064,2064,2064,5342,3588,5341,3739,620,620,3844,2591,1722,5174,2532,3588,975,3122,3588,3200],[223,3588,5471,1731,4183,2556,1473,1473,3588,2962,591,591,846,2596,2596,846,2041],[4771,2532,5442,5442,5442,3739,1063,436,436,436,436,2251,3056],[1722,1473,4413,627,3762,3762,3854,3854,1473,235,3956,1459,1473,3049,3049,3049,3049,3049,846,846],[1161,3588,2962,3936,3936,1473,2532,1743,1473,2443,2443,1223,1473,3588,2782,4135,4135,4135,4135,2532,3956,3588,1484,191,191,191,2532,4506,4506,4506,1537,4750,4750,3023,3023,3023],[3588,3588,2962,4506,4506,1473,575,3956,4190,2041,2532,4982,4982,4982,1519,846,2032,932,3739,3739,3739,3588,1391,165